<p>A few notes.  Trust in society is an irrational to the self or selfless behaviour, benefiting others with no clear guarantee of return.  Neither submission or cooperation reflects trust.  Trust may be displayed between immediate family members, parents, children, and possibly grandparents or first cousins, this is present in too many animals to count and is separate from society.</p>
